---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Contact | Z Best Media"
  description="Contact Z Best Media for enterprise command platform strategy, governance architecture, and operational transformation planning."
  path="/contact"
>
  <section class="grid gap-5">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold leading-tight">Contact</h1>
    <p class="text-muted max-w-[75ch]">
      If you are evaluating a platform for campaign command, content operations, intelligence workflows, or governance enforcement, we can
      start with a strategic brief designed for decision-makers and operators. The brief is practical and outcome-focused. We review your
      current delivery model, identify structural bottlenecks, and map control gaps that create avoidable risk. You receive a concrete
      plan for sequencing platform adoption while protecting active business operations and stakeholder confidence.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-10 rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface p-6 grid gap-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Direct Contact</h2>
    <p class="text-muted">
      Phone: <a class="hover:text-text" href="tel:+12136328384">(213) 632-8384</a><br />
      Email: <a class="hover:text-text" href="mailto:hello@zbestmedia.com">hello@zbestmedia.com</a>
    </p>
    <p class="text-muted max-w-[72ch]">
      We respond with scoped next steps, recommended participants, and a prep checklist to make your first session efficient. If your team
      is currently handling an active incident or high-priority launch, include that context and we will prioritize accordingly.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-10 grid gap-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">What to Expect in the Strategic Brief</h2>
    <p class="text-muted max-w-[75ch]">
      We begin with business objectives, critical timelines, and known constraints. From there we review operating workflows for planning,
      production, approvals, publishing, and reporting. We map where coordination cost is highest and where governance evidence is weakest.
      The output is a phased recommendation set with priority levels, implementation sequencing, and risk notes. This allows leadership to
      make resourcing decisions with a realistic view of impact and complexity.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-10 grid gap-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Who Should Join</h2>
    <p class="text-muted max-w-[75ch]">
      The most effective sessions include one executive sponsor, one operations lead, one technical owner, and one governance or compliance
      representative. This mix ensures that strategy, execution, and control requirements are aligned early. When those roles are present,
      teams can move from diagnosis to decision in one working session. If your structure differs, we can still adapt, but decision speed
      improves when cross-functional ownership is represented.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-10 grid gap-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Engagement Models</h2>
    <p class="text-muted max-w-[75ch]">
      We support focused advisory engagements, implementation tracks, and multi-phase transformation programs. Advisory engagements are
      ideal when you need architecture or governance decisions quickly. Implementation tracks are best when your team is ready to launch a
      defined scope within an existing platform timeline. Transformation programs combine workflow redesign, control activation, and
      capability transfer for long-term operating maturity. Each model includes measurable milestones and clear ownership boundaries.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-10 grid gap-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Immediate Next Step</h2>
    <p class="text-muted max-w-[75ch]">
      Start with a strategic brief so we can define your highest-value first move. The fastest path to progress is clarity on sequence,
      not breadth of ambition. Reach us directly at <a class="hover:text-text" href="tel:+12136328384">(213) 632-8384</a> or
      <a class="hover:text-text" href="mailto:hello@zbestmedia.com"> hello@zbestmedia.com</a>.
    </p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="tel:+12136328384" class="rounded-xl bg-gold px-5 py-3 text-bg font-semibold">Call Now</a>
      <a href="mailto:hello@zbestmedia.com" class="rounded-xl border border-border px-5 py-3">Email Us</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
